--[[
	Day/night look (client grade). ReplicatedStorage.Config.DayCycle  --  PROPOSED for 2.36 (sky-2360), not yet live.
	Generated by tools/sky-2360/gen_config.py from tools/sky-2360/presets.py; edit those and regenerate.
	Read by Controllers.World.DayCycle (and the new Controllers.World.SkyMotion for Motion). Wiring: docs/Sky-and-Lighting.md.

	Owner rules (2026-11-21): nights are dark but readable (ambient and exposure up, contrast down vs 2.16; the darkness
	comes from contrast with lamps and windows). Autumn is permanent; Winter / Spring / Summer / Nightmare Nights are
	events (workspace attribute NHSeason). Seven keys: Dawn, Morning, Day, Golden, Dusk, Night, Witching (0-4 h).

	Compatible with the 2.16 controller: Keys, Looks (Ambient ... Tint, Bloom) and Skies.Schedule/Sets/BlueMoon keep
	their shapes. The 2.36 controller adds: ColorShiftTop/Bottom, EnvDiffuse/EnvSpecular, Clouds, BloomSize/Threshold,
	SunRays; Seasons; Moon modifiers (weighted by NightWeight); the one merged grade (FullMoon/MoonPhases stop writing
	their own); and Skies.Preload (only the shown and next set are preloaded, event sets only during their event).
]]

